<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SA Breweries half year profit jumps.</title>
<headline>SA Breweries half year profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     185.2	 vs 162.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 65.0	  vs 57.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast earnings per share on a range of 167-182 cents and a dividend of 60-64 cents.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   553.0	 vs 475.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 1.202 billion vs 1.047 billion</p>
<p>    Tax			 415	   vs 390</p>
<p>    After tax		 823	   vs 711</p>
<p>    Turnover	     17.155 billion vs 14.807 billion</p>
<p>Div payable December 31</p>
<p>on register November 29</p>
<p>Full name: South African Breweries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - SAB is the world's fourth biggest brewer.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003  Attrib income</p>
</text>
